/*
	The native table `GAZLCmd` registers, as Impala prototypes. `import "natives.impala"` and every call
	is checked at Impala compile time, with a caret on the offending argument:

	    error[E406]: Argument type mismatch for argument 1 when calling printInt (float vs expected int)

	This replaces `nativeCallbackSignatures.gazl`, a `; signature`-only file that existed solely so
	`gazl-validate` could cross-check it after the fact. Retired 2026-08-05 with the validator: a
	prototype the compiler reads beats a manifest a separate tool compares against, and this one cannot
	drift out of the language it describes. Unused entries cost nothing - `--dead-strip` drops them, and
	an `extern native` emits no code or data of its own either way.

	Keep entries in the same order as the host registration tables (`tools/GAZLCmd.cpp`, `src/GAZL.cpp`)
	so additions are easy to diff. A host with a different table wants its own file like this one.
*/

extern native abort()
extern native assertFail(pointer message)
extern native printInt(int value)
extern native printFloat(float value)
extern native print(pointer text)
extern native printLF()
extern native input(int maxCount, pointer buffer) returns int got
extern native atan2(float y, float x) returns float r
extern native sqrt(float x) returns float r
extern native log(float x) returns float r
